{"agent_id":"pp3g-cHEZ-read-only-follow-up-process-review-hy3-for-issue-334","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-09T22:50:08.512294064Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f5cf8b37-fe5e-4123-9318-20282967be6e","comment_uuid":"543080af-2a08-4086-aa80-4de325e28d83","author":"pp3g-cHEZ-read-only-follow-up-process-review-hy3-for-issue-334","content":"## Review Summary: TRIPN CHANGE VALIDATES + REFINES #330 — DOES NOT RESOLVE #331 MUST-FIX — ASES ADOPTION = MORE READY WITH AMENDMENTS (3 MUST FIX)\n\nRead-only follow-up process review. Subjects: #330 process finding (checkpointing-as-durability; read-only roles treat comment+sync as their commit), my own #331 verdict (SOUND WITH AMENDMENTS; 3 MUST-FIX), and the tripn-astro permission-change finding docs/research/read-only-role-crosslink-allowlist.md (read per #334 summary — see WHAT-NOT-TESTED: full 347-line doc not in this worktree's git). Independence preserved (§5.6): only #330/#331/#334 read; no sibling sub-issues read.\n\n=== ITEM 2: COMPARISON vs #330 / #331 ===\n\n(2a) Narrow allowlist vs #330 read-only-durability principle — EXTENDS / REFINES (partially).\n#330 §4 proposed read-only roles hold broad 'crosslink *'. Tripn deliberately chose narrow Option B (issue comment/show, session status, knowledge search/list/add/edit/delete; auditor + sync). This is the disciplined operationalization #330 should have specified — it validates the principle (read-only roles need a crosslink durability primitive) while adding the structural boundary #330 omitted. BUT it is a PARTIAL implementation: the reviewer gets comment but NOT sync, so the comment+sync primitive is half-built for the reviewer. Principle validated; grant incomplete.\n\n(2b) Resolves or leaves open #331 MUST-FIX #3 (comment+sync vs §6.5 sync-rollback)? — LEAVES OPEN + MAKES MORE ACUTE.\n#331 MUST-FIX #3: pin/verify the read-only comment+sync primitive against §6.5 sync-rollback (sync documented as data-lossy on stale hub checkpoints; safe only on binaries carrying the ade6146b fail-closed guard). Tripn grants the AUDITOR 'crosslink sync' explicitly — so the exact command #331 flagged is now a LIVE granted command for a read-only role. The precondition (ade6146b guard) is therefore now a real verification requirement, not hypothetical. The reviewer lacks sync entirely, so cannot even attempt the primitive. Net: MUST-FIX #3 is UNRESOLVED and now applies to a deployed grant.\n\n(2c) Option A vs B (structural vs aspirational boundary) vs #330 reasoning — REFINES.\n#330's 'crosslink *' was aspirational/Option-A-ish. Tripn's explicit Option B (repo-immutability, preserve structural boundary, referencing agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement-reviewed.md) is the structurally-disciplined version #330 lacked. Aligns with #330 intent, adds the boundary discipline #330 omitted. CAVEAT: the Option B rationale is undercut by the knowledge add/edit/delete grant (a parallel write surface NOT covered by repo-immutability) — see Item 3.\n\n(2d) Residual gaps B-E — which are natural ASES next steps?\n- B (continuation-branch audits): ADOPT — needs the sync grant to be durable.\n- C (auditor prompt template): ADOPT — ASES auditor.md must be updated to use the new sync capability + comment+sync primitive.\n- D (read-only heartbeat): ADOPT — directly implements my #331 two-layer-liveness proposal (mechanical heartbeat + position). High value.\n- E (read-only git): REJECT for ASES — #330 §4 explicitly rejected scoped git write for read-only roles (defeats the read-only guarantee). ASES already has the principled answer; treat E as out-of-scope, not a gap to close.\n\n(2e) Validates or complicates 'position stream is ground truth' (two-layer liveness; watcher reads hub events.log)? — VALIDATES principle, COMPLICATES operationalization.\nValidates: read-only roles can now emit durable hub positions — necessary for the position stream to include read-only output. Complicates: (1) reviewer can't sync → reviewer positions absent from hub stream → a watcher reading hub agent-ref events.log (my #331 proposal) won't see them → two-layer liveness broken for reviewers until the sync gap closes; (2) knowledge add/edit/delete creates a SECOND persistence path → 'ground truth' risks splitting between hub comments and knowledge store → must declare hub comments canonical, knowledge secondary.\n\n=== ITEM 3: CRITIQUE OF TRIPN FINDING ON ITS OWN MERITS ===\n\nDirection is sound. Specific risks:\n1. REVIEWER-SYNC GAP (incomplete primitive): reviewer can comment but not sync → durability depends on a relay (orchestrator/auditor) → partially REINTRODUCES the single-point-of-failure the change was meant to remove. Either grant reviewer 'crosslink sync' or define+verify the relay mechanism against §6.5.\n2. KNOWLEDGE WRITE SURFACE: granting read-only roles knowledge add/edit/DELETE is a write surface. 'delete' is especially dangerous (a reviewer could delete shared knowledge). Option B preserves REPO-immutability but NOT knowledge-store immutability — the Option B rationale doesn't address this. Recommend: scope to add (and own-entry edit); drop delete, or namespace writes to the role's own findings.\n3. SESSION-STATUS-WITHOUT-SYNC STALE HAZARD: reviewer can read session status (local) but can't sync; if it posts a comment and reads session status as 'confirmation', it gets FALSE durability confidence. The missing sync creates a false-confidence hazard.\n4. AUDITOR 'crosslink sync' EXPOSES §6.5 RISK: the auditor now runs the exact command documented as data-lossy on stale hub checkpoints — must verify the ade6146b fail-closed guard on the binaries the auditor executes.\n\nWhat I would change: grant reviewer sync (or document+verify relay); scope knowledge writes (drop delete); add read-only heartbeat as first-class; verify auditor sync against §6.5 guard; declare hub comments the canonical position stream vs knowledge.\n\n=== ITEM 4: VERDICT ON ASES ADOPTION READINESS ===\n\n(a) MORE READY, WITH AMENDMENTS. The tripn change is real-world evidence the #330 principle is deployable and refines it into a disciplined narrow allowlist. It surfaces the concrete sharp edges (reviewer sync, knowledge surface, heartbeat) ASES must close. It does NOT resolve #331 MUST-FIX items; it makes #331 MUST-FIX #3 live for the auditor.\n\nConcrete amendments to the #330 finding:\n- Amend #330 §4 ('read-only roles hold crosslink *') → specify NARROW allowlist (Option B): issue comment/show, session status, knowledge search/list/(scoped add/edit), and (auditor) sync. Not full 'crosslink *'.\n- Add explicit reviewer-sync requirement: the read-only durability primitive is comment+sync; if sync isn't granted to the reviewer the primitive is incomplete — grant it or define+verify the relay against §6.5.\n- Add knowledge-write-surface caveat: knowledge add/edit/delete is a write surface; scope it (drop delete) and don't let it dilute 'position stream is ground truth' (hub comments canonical).\n- Carry forward #331 MUST-FIX #3: verify granted 'crosslink sync' (auditor) against §6.5 ade6146b fail-closed guard before relying on it as the durability primitive.\n\nConcrete amendments to the tripn implementation (for ASES mirror per §5.5):\n- Grant reviewer 'crosslink sync' (or document+verify relay).\n- Scope knowledge delete (and consider edit scoping).\n- Add read-only heartbeat (gap D) as first-class.\n- Mirror the narrow allowlist + #330/#331 amendments BIDIRECTIONALLY per §5.5 (ASES ← tripn narrow allowlist; tripn-astro ← #330/#331 playbook amendments: atomic §5.3 rewrite, rate-bound cap, sync-guard verification). One-sided landing = §5.5 drift.\n\n=== MUST FIX (blocking for ASES adoption) ===\n- Reviewer-sync gap: read-only durability primitive (comment+sync) incomplete for reviewer (no sync grant). Either grant reviewer 'crosslink sync' or define+verify the relay against §6.5 sync-rollback before ASES adopts. [tripn doc / ASES agent defs]\n- #331 MUST-FIX #3 still OPEN + now LIVE: verify the auditor's granted 'crosslink sync' against the §6.5 ade6146b fail-closed guard (sync documented data-lossy on stale hub checkpoints). Tripn makes this a real granted command. [ASES agent defs / §6.5]\n- Knowledge write-surface scoping: read-only roles granted knowledge add/edit/DELETE — 'delete' erodes the read-only guarantee in the knowledge dimension (Option B only covers repo-immutability). Scope to add (own-entry edit); drop delete or namespace. [tripn doc / ASES agent defs]\n\n=== SHOULD CONSIDER (non-blocking) ===\n- Declare hub comments the CANONICAL position stream; knowledge store secondary, so 'position stream is ground truth' isn't split. [playbook §5.8 / tripn doc]\n- Adopt gaps B (continuation-branch audits) + C (auditor prompt template); adopt D (read-only heartbeat) per #331 two-layer liveness.\n- Treat gap E (read-only git) as OUT OF SCOPE for ASES — #330 §4 already rejected scoped git write; don't reopen.\n- Mirror bidirectionally per §5.5: ASES adopts tripn narrow allowlist; tripn-astro receives #330/#331 playbook amendments. One-sided = §5.5 drift.\n- Document that reviewer comments are NOT durable until synced; don't let session status imply durability.\n\n=== NITS ===\n- Tripn doc references agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement-reviewed.md for A/B; ASES should cross-link the same reasoning so the two repos don't diverge on the boundary rationale.\n- 'positions durable at composition time' is a good phrase; ASES playbook §5.8 should adopt it explicitly.\n\n=== NOTABLE POSITIVES ===\n- Real-world validation: tripn change is empirical evidence (observed drops 9Lg8-3eZm/9Lg8-R3da/9Lg8-dLdE/9Lg8-GpBh) that read-only roles need self-persistence — exactly #330's premise. Strong, evidence-based.\n- Disciplined Option B (narrow over full 'crosslink *') preserves the structural boundary #330 omitted — the right instinct, constructively refining #330.\n- Explicitly distinguishes tool-denial (A) vs repo-immutability (B) read-only semantics — a clean conceptual contribution ASES should adopt.\n- Surfaces its own residual gaps B-E honestly — good adversarial hygiene.\n\n=== WHAT-NOT-TESTED ===\n- Could NOT read the full 347-line tripn doc: not in this worktree's git object store (git log --all found no such path; commits 8612f766/79b35eac absent here) and filesystem access is restricted to the worktree. Analysis uses the detailed summary in #334's description + my #331 verdict + #330. The allowlist command list, Option A/B rationale, and gaps B-E are taken from the task summary, not verified against source.\n- Did NOT verify whether tripn-astro has an auto-sync-on-comment or defined relay that would make the reviewer's missing 'sync' moot — the reviewer-sync critique assumes none exists; if one does, the gap is documentation, not capability.\n- Did NOT verify the ade6146b fail-closed guard is present on the binaries the auditor/reviewer run (the §6.5 precondition) — live #331 MUST-FIX #3, unverified here.\n- Did NOT read tripn-astro reviewer.md/auditor.md to confirm the allowlist is deployed as described — the tripn doc is the cited source, not independently confirmed.\n- Did NOT test knowledge add/edit/delete as a read-only role to confirm scoping/delete behavior.\n- Independence preserved (§5.6): read only #330/#331/#334; no sibling review sub-issues read.\n\n=== VERDICT ===\nTripn-astro's permission change VALIDATES the #330 principle and REFINES it (narrow Option B over broad 'crosslink *'). It does NOT resolve the #331 MUST-FIX items — it makes #331 MUST-FIX #3 a live granted command (auditor sync) and leaves the reviewer's primitive incomplete. ASES adoption is MORE READY but gated on 3 MUST FIX: close the reviewer-sync gap, verify auditor sync against the §6.5 ade6146b guard, and scope the knowledge write surface (drop delete). Mirror bidirectionally per §5.5.","created_at":"2026-08-09T22:50:08.500612229Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:JIoMOqC6/tle3OmcQag47jWRccYVa5ST0gVf6qBrwK8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguzVuH1/PlQmiHGNWjp/wjxX5d89/1x3FWVvwKUZbossAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAdLFyKDl/wkxhUCjsQl8Aq1KoOcC3KUW5VubZykrGkgMVEfO4wylK6ehl0zy9Z470WQHwqIAGo8HINy3tW2o0Dw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:JIoMOqC6/tle3OmcQag47jWRccYVa5ST0gVf6qBrwK8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguzVuH1/PlQmiHGNWjp/wjxX5d89/1x3FWVvwKUZbossAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP7oJP+Nv19MkMR92pFpePUqrKTmC3HO77TZc+COlnUd92N0XY0kPeS7MRWgw5umxD7giwmQJeZOJY0bdA6CEAs="}
